  "classification": "actual all-stride quadratic-carrier boundary theorem; narrow gauge representation obstructions; focused circuit-locator applicability audit; no whole-query improvement",
  "model_authorization": "User authorized parallel Sol 6.1 research; three existing gpt-6.1-sol agents reused.",
  "whole_family_soft_linear_query_acquired": false,
  "general_query_bound": "soft O(m^(3/2)), unchanged",
  "main_theorem": "For literal offsets and local gamma order R>8m^2, every fieldwise nonidentity scalar shift leaves at least ceil((m-1)/4) dangling deduplicated nodes. All shifts simultaneous, including advised choices; no new deletion.",
  "arithmetic_reason": "Exact low image N(Squares-1) and quadratic-character identity |S minus (S+h)|=(m+1-chi(h)-chi(-h))/4; two-node fibers for nonzero shifts divisible by m.",
  "descent_scope": "Regular representative-independent homogeneous fixed-carrier descent must zero the boundary; higher jets and powered-node compatibility consequences explicit. Not an operation lower bound.",
  "gauge_scope": "Matched-base contiguous product gauges need linearly many blocks; minimal q-gauge has unpaid residue payload and nilpotent homogeneous operator. Sums, unmatched bases and nearlinear sharing remain possible.",
  "actual_nonvacuity": "Canonical fixed-length two-endpoint-unit branch coexists with density and exclusive residues by union of bad-input counts against the same original majority supply.",
  "literature_scope": "Inspected primary theorem interfaces do not provide uniform soft O(s+d) vector-SLP locator acquisition. ECCC primary gap notice respected. No exhaustive or generic impossibility claimed.",
  "missing_work": "Restriction-stable soft O(m) acquisition of quotient forcing, channel remainder, exact collision locator or sufficient factor query; full bit/controller and Lean composition.",
  "verification_scope": "Classical proofs and final-byte independent reviews. No new native Lean declaration, build or benchmark.",
